      "refersTo": "project-region-neutral",
      "description": "The inserted area's project, owned by the face region color.",
      "html": "<article class=\"ds-plate\"><h3 class=\"ds-plate__title\">TrainLog</h3><p>An offline-first training PWA.</p><dl class=\"ds-spec\"><dt>Stack</dt><dd>React, TypeScript, PWA</dd></dl><a class=\"ds-plate__link\" href=\"#\">Source</a></article>",
      "css": ".ds-plate{max-width:520px;padding:32px;background:#F3D250;color:#16324A;border-radius:3px;font-family:Archivo,system-ui,sans-serif}.ds-plate__title{font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:780;font-variation-settings:\"wdth\" 118;letter-spacing:-.035em;line-height:1;margin:0 0 16px}.ds-spec{display:grid;grid-template-columns:max-content 1fr;gap:8px 20px;margin:24px 0 0;padding-top:18px;border-top:1px solid #16324A38;font-size:.9rem}.ds-spec dt{color:#3E4A2A}.ds-spec dd{margin:0}.ds-plate__link{display:inline-block;margin-top:24px;color:inherit;font-weight:650;text-underline-offset:.22em}.ds-plate__link:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #16324A;outline-offset:3px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Project Plate (default)",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "project-plate-neutral",
      "description": "Projects not owned by the active area: ground-2 with a hairline.",
      "html": "<article class=\"ds-card\"><h3>ChangeSmith</h3><p>Plugins that make coding agents work like a careful engineer.</p></article>",
      "css": ".ds-card{max-width:520px;padding:32px;background:#F7F7F7;color:#16324A;border:1px solid #16324A2E;border-radius:3px;font-family:Archivo,system-ui,sans-serif}.ds-card h3{font-size:2.2rem;font-weight:780;font-variation-settings:\"wdth\" 118;letter-spacing:-.035em;line-height:1;margin:0 0 16px}.ds-card p{margin:0;max-width:46ch}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Modular Chassis",
    "overview": "The site is one engineered instrument. The neutral face is the chassis: a light-gray plate with a sticky rail, the 10-second line, and four numbered slots (01–04). Inserting a module (Full-stack & Product, AI & Agents, Data & Analytics, 3D & Engineering design) changes the whole face: palette, display face, background texture, hover material and seat timing. Ejecting restores the neutral face intact. The chassis carries all content; choosing a module is optional.\n\nEvery face redefines the same set of roles (ground, ground-2, plate, ink, ink-2, signal, on-signal, cta, on-cta, region, on-region, on-region-2, rule, display face, display width/weight/tracking, a size multiplier `k`, texture, seat duration and easing). Layout reads only the roles, which is how five faces share one grid. Hardware cues are real structure: hairline rules are the mounting rails, slot numbers are the navigation, the five-color edge on each slot is that module's palette, set like a screen-printed legend.\n\nThe system refuses the dark-neon developer portfolio and the skill-bar résumé page. Depth is layer overlap, never soft shadow.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Five faces, one grid; faces swap materials, never positions.",
      "Each face's palette owns whole regions (a project plate, the close section), not scattered accents.",
      "Seating motion has mass and a per-face rhythm; reduced motion cuts instantly.",
      "Lining, tabular numerals everywhere; slot numbers and years in condensed light Archivo.",
      "Flat plates with 1px rules and 3px milled corners."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Region Ownership Rule",
        "body": "The active face's region color owns whole blocks: the inserted area's project plate and the close section. It never appears as a scattered accent over another face's ground.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Snow Is Not a Ground Rule",
        "body": "Full-stack's #E7E3D4 is a legend color only; the Full-stack face is never a beige ground with brown ink.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Pinned Palette Rule",
        "body": "Palette values are owner-pinned and change only with the owner. The AI palette is approved as built and stays exactly as is.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Size Multiplier Rule",
        "body": "Display sizes are one clamp scale multiplied by the face's `k` (neutral 1, Full-stack 1.04, AI 0.86, Data 0.9, 3D 0.8), so wider faces shrink and the copy block keeps one height.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Lining Numerals Rule",
        "body": "The whole document sets `lining-nums tabular-nums`; slot numbers and years never use oldstyle figures.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Doto Is Display Only Rule",
        "body": "The dot-matrix face sets display roles only; Data body text stays Archivo.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Registration Rule",
        "body": "All five faces share the grid to the pixel. Switching faces changes only what content is made of; it never moves the slot row or reflows the layout. Reordering projects by active area is the only sanctioned change, and it happens below the fold.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Seated Plate Rule",
        "body": "The 6px offset plate is reserved for the seated state of a slot. It is a real layer with the ground's own color and an ink hairline, not a shadow, and it does not decorate resting elements.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No Glow Rule",
        "body": "No soft drop shadows, no glow, no blur.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ballistics Rule",
        "body": "Every reskin moves with mass and the face's own seat timing. No linear fades, no instant swaps, except the immediate cut under reduced motion.",
        "section": "components"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do define every new face or surface through the shared role set, so layout code reads only roles.",
      "Do keep the copy block at its single shared height so the slot row registers across faces.",
      "Do let the active palette own whole regions (project plate, close section).",
      "Do give each face its own hover material and seat timing.",
      "Do keep every text/ground pairing at WCAG AA and focus indicators at 3:1 or better against their ground.",
      "Do render pending links as dashed ink-2 text that explains itself on tap."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't move layout between faces.",
      "Don't use soft drop shadows or glow; depth is layer overlap.",
      "Don't put kicker or eyebrow labels above headings.",
      "Don't make a pending link look live.",
      "Don't use a beige ground or brown ink on the Full-stack face.",
      "Don't add hardware costume (screws, knobs, LEDs) that does not map to structure or state.",
      "Don't use dark-plus-neon glow, skill-percentage bars or contribution counters."
    ]
  }
}
